\[ \text{Total Interest} = \text{Principal} \times \text{Interest Rate} \]
\[ \text{Total Interest} = 3650 \times 0.10 \]
\[ \text{Total Interest} = 365 \]

Next, we divide the total interest by the number of months to find the monthly payment.

\[ \text{Monthly Payment} = \frac{\text{Total Interest}}{\text{Number of Months}} \]
\[ \text{Monthly Payment} = \frac{365}{5} \]
\[ \text{Monthly Payment} = 73 \]

Therefore, Karan has to pay $73 per month.

