\[ 40 \times 2 = 80 \text{ hotdogs} \]

The caterer prepared 36 hotdogs, so the number of hotdogs short is:

\[ 80 - 36 = 44 \text{ hotdogs} \]

Since each guest wants 2 hotdogs, the number of guests who did not get a second hotdog is:

\[ \frac{44}{2} = 22 \text{ guests} \]

Therefore, the number of guests who did not get a second hotdog is 22.
