answer:  To determine how long it will take Bob to dig the hole, we first need to calculate the volume of the hole. The volume \( V \) of a rectangular prism (which is the shape of the hole) is given by the formula:

\[ V = \text{length} \times \text{width} \times \text{depth} \]

Given the dimensions of the hole:
- Length = 6 feet
- Width = 4 feet
- Depth = 3 feet

So, the volume \( V \) is:

\[ V = 6 \times 4 \times 3 = 72 \text{ cubic feet} \]

Next, we know that it takes Bob 3 seconds to shovel one cubic foot of earth. Therefore, the total time \( T \) required to dig the hole is:

\[ T = \text{Volume} \times \text{Time per cubic foot} \]

\[ T = 72 \text{ cubic feet} \times 3 \text{ seconds per cubic foot} = 216 \text{ seconds} \]

It will take Bob 216 seconds to dig the hole.
