\[ \text{Rate} = \frac{3 \text{ pages}}{10 \text{ minutes}} = 0.3 \text{ pages per minute} \]

Next, we use this rate to find the time it takes to read 18 pages:
\[ \text{Time} = \frac{18 \text{ pages}}{0.3 \text{ pages per minute}} = \frac{18}{0.3} \text{ minutes} \]

To simplify the division, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by 10:
\[ \text{Time} = \frac{18 \times 10}{0.3 \times 10} = \frac{180}{3} = 60 \text{ minutes} \]

Therefore, James spends 60 minutes reading.

Answer: \( \boxed{60} \) minutes
