Soledad needs to hike 9,300 miles in total. She plans to hike 7,500 miles. The difference she needs to hike is:
\[ 9300 - 7500 = 1800 \text{ miles} \]

To find out how many more miles per day she needs to hike, we divide the additional distance by the number of days in June:
\[ \frac{1800}{30} = 60 \text{ miles per day} \]

Therefore, Soledad needs to hike 60 more miles per day to complete her journey on time.

