\[ 1.5 \text{ hours} = 1.5 \times 60 = 90 \text{ minutes} \]

Now, we calculate the number of 30-minute episodes Frankie watched on Wednesday:
\[ \frac{90 \text{ minutes}}{30 \text{ minutes/episode}} = 3 \text{ episodes} \]

So, Frankie watched 3 30-minute episodes on Wednesday.
