   \]

2. Determine the speed of the car in the slow lane:
   The car in the slow lane is traveling at half the speed of the car in the fast lane.
   \[
   \text{Speed of slow lane} = \frac{60 \text{ miles/hour}}{2} = 30 \text{ miles/hour}
   \]

3. Calculate the time taken by the car in the slow lane to cover the same distance:
   \[
   \text{Time} = \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Speed}} = \frac{480 \text{ miles}}{30 \text{ miles/hour}} = 16 \text{ hours}
   \]

Therefore, the car in the slow lane took 16 hours to cover the same distance.
