     \]
   - The temperature decrease is:
     \[
     3 \text{ intervals} \times 2 \text{ degrees/interval} = 6 \text{ degrees}
     \]
   - Subtracting this from the current temperature:
     \[
     55 \text{ degrees} - 6 \text{ degrees} = 49 \text{ degrees}
     \]

Therefore, the house's final temperature is 49 degrees.

