\[
\text{Discount amount} = 0.10 \times 30.00 = 3.00
\]

**Step 4: Subtract the discount amount from the total cost to get the final cost.**

\[
\text{Final cost} = 30.00 - 3.00 = 27.00
\]

Therefore, Daniel has to spend $27.00 on all the items he wants to buy.

