answer:  First, we need to calculate the volume of the pool in cubic feet. The volume \( V \) of a rectangular prism (which is the shape of the pool) is given by the formula:

\[ V = \text{length} \times \text{width} \times \text{depth} \]

Given the dimensions of the pool:
- Length = 25 feet
- Width = 14 feet
- Depth = 4 feet

So, the volume \( V \) is:

\[ V = 25 \, \text{feet} \times 14 \, \text{feet} \times 4 \, \text{feet} \]

\[ V = 1400 \, \text{cubic feet} \]

Next, we need to convert the volume from cubic feet to gallons. The conversion factor is 1 cubic foot = 7.48 gallons. Therefore, the volume in gallons is:

\[ \text{Volume in gallons} = \text{Volume in cubic feet} \times 7.48 \]

\[ \text{Volume in gallons} = 1400 \, \text{cubic feet} \times 7.48 \, \text{gallons/cubic foot} \]

\[ \text{Volume in gallons} = 10472 \, \text{gallons} \]

Now, we need to calculate the total volume of water needed by multiplying the volume in gallons by 5.9:

\[ \text{Total volume} = 10472 \, \text{gallons} \times 5.9 \]

\[ \text{Total volume} = 61760 \, \text{gallons} \]

Finally, we calculate the cost to fill the pool. The cost per gallon is $0.10, so the total cost is:

\[ \text{Total cost} = \text{Total volume} \times \text{Cost per gallon} \]

\[ \text{Total cost} = 61760 \, \text{gallons} \times 0.10 \, \text{$gallon} \]

\[ \text{Total cost} = \$6176 \]

The cost to fill the pool is $6176.
