   Abraham sold another 1/4 of his land for $30.
   \[
   \text{Land sold in second sale} = \frac{40}{4} = 10 \text{ square meters}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Remaining land after second sale} = 40 - 10 = 30 \text{ square meters}
   \]

3. **Remaining land after the second sale:**
   \[
   \text{Remaining land} = 30 \text{ square meters}
   \]

4. **Earnings from the remaining land:**
   Abraham sold the remaining land for $3 per square meter.
   \[
   \text{Earnings from remaining land} = 30 \times 3 = 90 \text{ dollars}
   \]

5. **Total earnings:**
   Add the earnings from all sales.
   \[
   \text{Total earnings} = \text{Earnings from first sale} + \text{Earnings from second sale} + \text{Earnings from remaining land}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Total earnings} = 50 + 30 + 90 = 170 \text{ dollars}
   \]

Therefore, Abraham will be able to earn $170 after selling all his unused land.

