**Step 1: Calculate John's new speaking speed after training.**

John's normal speaking speed is 150 words per minute (WPM). After training, his speed is 2.5 times faster than his starting speed.

\[ \text{New speed} = 150 \text{ WPM} \times 2.5 = 375 \text{ WPM} \]

**Step 2: Determine the total number of words in 10 pages.**

Each page has 450 words. Therefore, for 10 pages:

\[ \text{Total words} = 10 \text{ pages} \times 450 \text{ words per page} = 4500 \text{ words} \]

**Step 3: Calculate the time required to speak the total number of words at his new speed.**

