   \[
   \text{Revenue from cupcakes} = 20 \text{ cupcakes} \times \$2 \text{ per cupcake} = \$40
   \]

2. Calculate the total revenue from selling cookies:
   \[
   \text{Revenue from cookies} = 40 \text{ cookies} \times \$1 \text{ per cookie} = \$40
   \]

3. Add the total revenue from cupcakes and cookies to get the total revenue:
   \[
   \text{Total revenue} = \$40 + \$40 = \$80
   \]

4. Subtract the cost of the trays from the total revenue:
   \[
   \text{Cost of trays} = 5 \text{ trays} \times \$4 \text{ per tray} = \$20
   \]
   \[
   \text{Money left} = \$80 - \$20 = \$60
   \]

Therefore, Frances has \$60 left.
